%S A401829 2,2,2,4,0,4,4,4,4,2,10,-2,6,8,0,10,10,-2,20,12,-12,-18,16,0,20,-6,22,
%T A401829 0,36,2,6,-10,-22,-28,16,4,36,-26,30,12,8,6,34,16,-24,-8,-12,4,20,-6,
%U A401829 30,16,6,-2,8,4,4,-16,-14,10,8,-12,44,32,-18,10,28,30,-20,-24,26,0,52,-16,44,-2
%N A401829 Net change in the firing population from generation n to generation n+1 of a four-state cellular automaton on the infinite square lattice (rule B2/S34/C4, see Comments), starting with two horizontally adjacent firing cells and all other cells ready.
%C A401829 The states are 0 (ready), 1 (firing), 2 and 3. Updates are synchronous and count firing cells among the eight cells horizontally, vertically or diagonally adjacent to a cell (its Moore neighbors). A ready cell becomes 1 if the count is 2, and stays 0 otherwise. A firing cell stays firing iff the count is 3 or 4; otherwise it becomes 2. States 2 and 3 become 3 and 0, respectively. Initially only (0,0) and (1,0) fire.
%C A401829 In the code B2/S34/C4, B2 (birth) means that a ready cell fires when the count is 2, S34 (survival) that a firing cell keeps firing when the count is 3 or 4, and C4 that there are 4 states. Rules given by such a code are called "Generations" rules; the program MCell writes the code as survival/birth/states, here 34/2/4 (see the Wójtowicz link).
%C A401829 Every term is even: reflection about x = 1/2 pairs the firing cells in each generation, so consecutive firing populations have even difference.
%C A401829 It appears that the terms, colored by n mod 4, form four crossing bands for 0 <= n < 20000; see the plot.
%C A401829 See A401828 for the perpetual rake factories at the leading fronts and a verified two-generation family tree of rakes.
%H A401829 Alper Ferudun, <a href="/A401829/b401829.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..9999</a>
%H A401829 Alper Ferudun, <a href="/A401828/a401828.txt">Additional comments</a>.
%H A401829 Alper Ferudun, <a href="/A401828/a401828.png">First differences colored by n mod 4</a>.
%H A401829 Alper Ferudun, <a href="/A401828/a401828_2.png">Leading-cap factory with period 192</a>.
