%H A401829 Alper Ferudun, <a href="/A401828/a401828_1.txt">Rust program</a>.
%H A401829 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/MooreNeighborhood.html">Moore Neighborhood</a>.
%H A401829 Mirek Wójtowicz, <a href="https://mcell.ca/pages/families.html#generations">Supported CA Families: Generations</a>, MCell.
%H A401829 <a href="/index/Ce#cell">Index entries for sequences related to cellular automata</a>.
%F A401829 a(n) = A401828(n+1) - A401828(n).
%e A401829 At generation 1 the firing cells are (0,-1), (1,-1), (0,1), (1,1): each was ready with the two initial firing cells as neighbors. The initial cells become state 2, so a(0) = 4 - 2 = 2.
%e A401829 At generation 2 the firing cells are (0,-2), (1,-2), (-1,0), (2,0), (0,2), (1,2), each born with two firing neighbors. The previous four firing cells become state 2, while (0,0) and (1,0) become state 3, so a(1) = 6 - 4 = 2.
